    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0128" n="12" xml:id="pg12"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.242.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Belden to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 6, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s instruction of May 29. Bolivian Government, through
                    notes exchanged with Legation, accepts abrogation of Article 34 of the Treaty of
                    Amity, Commerce and Navigation of May 13, 1858, to take effect July 1, 1916.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belden.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
